{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future","id":1391468,"title":"Can you get temporal refugees from the future?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-25T06:27:57-07:00","id":1391468,"title":"Can you get temporal refugees from the future?","content":"Can a mage create a routine where they wake up every morning and casts a spell to determine if he is in the present, or one of the myriad unwritten futures?<br /> <br /> And if he can; does anything stop him from thinking that if he's in the future there's a big chance this future won't be the one that becomes real so he'd better teleport back to the past and try and stick there as long as he can? Could you have a whole collective of the same mage from different potential futures living in the present and desperately trying to anchor themselves so they can live there permanently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T07:05:58-07:00","id":1391474,"title":"","content":"If this is ever a concern then you are not playing a game of Mage where time is functioning normally. The future is unwritten because it's the time that the present hasn't reached yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T07:47:04-07:00","id":1391480,"title":"","content":"While not mage, I had these two ideas for timetravellers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Eschaton the Cataclysm. You play as time travelers from different divergent future timelines, you survived your apocalypse by jumping back in time, maybe you can change things or maybe its inevitable and you wish to steer it to the end of your liking. Yours are the tools of the last stage of humanity which likely brought about its end.<br /> <br /> Vagrant: the Beyond You are alien to this world and play beings from different planets, dimensions, timelines, and time periods. Your advantages are mysterious of your kind, alien gifts to this world denizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T07:49:27-07:00","id":1391481,"title":"","content":"That doesn't really answer the question Satchel,<br /> <br /> What happens if a Mage sits down at their crystal ball and casts a spell to watch what they're up to tomorrow in the most probable future. Tomorrow!mage is sitting at his crystal ball casing a spell to check if they're in the present or the future. What does Today!Mage see Tomororw!Mage's spell say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-25-2020, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T09:35:27-07:00","id":1391492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future?p=1391481#post1391481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really answer the question Satchel,</div> </div> </div> </div>Then ask the question you want answered instead of its neighbor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens if a Mage sits down at their crystal ball and casts a spell to watch what they're up to tomorrow in the most probable future. Tomorrow!mage is sitting at his crystal ball casing a spell to check if they're in the present or the future. What does Today!Mage see Tomororw!Mage's spell say. </div> </div> </div>That they're in the present. Because that is when they will be when they cast the spell. They don't exist yet except as a simulation created by a spell, barring aberrant circumstances like Abyssal intervention and other Mysteries. Stuff registering as being from the future in the objective present is specifically a weird thing to find, as demonstrated by the most regular instances being from Atlantean ruins and archspells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T09:36:19-07:00","id":1391494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future?p=1391481#post1391481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really answer the question Satchel,<br /> <br /> What happens if a Mage sits down at their crystal ball and casts a spell to watch what they're up to tomorrow in the most probable future. Tomorrow!mage is sitting at his crystal ball casing a spell to check if they're in the present or the future. What does Today!Mage see Tomororw!Mage's spell say.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not looking at the future. You're looking at what might happen in the future. There is no Tomorrow!Mage further along in the timeline who can notice he's not actually in the present. You'll see what Today!Mage sees when Today!Mage finally arrives in the future to cast that spell.<br /> <br /> Edit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future?p=1391492#post1391492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then ask the question you want answered instead of its neighbor.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair you didn't answer any question at all. You gave a cryptic explanation that could be extrapolated into answers for those questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-25-2020, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T09:59:34-07:00","id":1391500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future?p=1391494#post1391494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair you didn't answer any question at all. You gave a cryptic explanation that could be extrapolated into answers for those questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that the framework in which people come from the future into the present is not the one Mage normally uses and defined what the future is within that framework. That is not cryptic just because the question lacked qualifiers that would make it make sense as something somebody who actually read the section on the Time Arcanum would ask instead of talking about teleporting to the past from potential futures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T06:47:26-07:00","id":1391672,"title":"","content":"<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future?p=1391481#post1391481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really answer the question Satchel,<br /> <br /> What happens if a Mage sits down at their crystal ball and casts a spell to watch what they're up to tomorrow in the most probable future. Tomorrow!mage is sitting at his crystal ball casing a spell to check if they're in the present or the future. What does Today!Mage see Tomororw!Mage's spell say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly a better way to address the core intent of the question is to look at a situation where a Time mage is using an Making version of Choose the Threads that is less divination and more &quot;I created multiple parallel timelines and will act differently in each and then pick which one to keep after the fact&quot; where there are multiple instances of the same &quot;present&quot; and further Time magic could be used to travel between these.<br /> <br /> Or for extra fun, Mind mages from the different variant timelines could be trying to mindcontrol the caster to make him pick THEIR timeline.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future?p=1391492#post1391492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then ask the question you want answered instead of its neighbor.<br /> <br /> That they're in the present. Because that is when they will be when they cast the spell. They don't exist yet except as a simulation created by a spell, barring aberrant circumstances like Abyssal intervention and other Mysteries. Stuff registering as being from the future in the objective present is specifically a weird thing to find, as demonstrated by the most regular instances being from Atlantean ruins and archspells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff registering as being FROM the future isn't that weird. Any Time 3+ mage can pull that off. And it highlights them and their actions in BIG NEON SPOTLIGHTS in Time Sight. The part that confuses people is that they think that there's a single &quot;present&quot;. For the timetraveller, the &quot;present&quot; is the time they cast their time travelling spell, and they are in the past. For everyone else, the current time is the &quot;present&quot; and the time traveler shows signs of significant temporal distortion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now something registering ITSELF as being IN or FROM the future , now that's weird.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T08:57:08-07:00","id":1391688,"title":"","content":"Is there anything to suggest whether &quot;natives&quot; to a time period that's not the present can tell they're not in the present, assuming they don't have direct contact with a time traveler? The 2nd edition core book says &quot;Mages who travel back in time and look forward find that the intervening span is still set&quot;--i.e. if you go back from 2020 to 2018 and then look ahead to 2019, you won't find multiple possible versions of 2019 like you normally would when looking into the future, instead you'll just see the same 2019 that was part of your past in 2020. But if some <i>other</i> mage around you in 2018 looks ahead to 2019, will the same be true for them, or will they see multiple possible versions of 2019 as usual? The wording might suggest this rule only applies to time travelers themselves, and I think it would also cause all sorts of problems if every time you traveled to the past, part of the way you'd be altering history would be that practically every other mage community around the world would soon learn they were just living in a sort of draft version of an altered past (one which could be undone by locating the time traveler and dispelling the magic that brought them there, which is said in the core book to revert history to the original version).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","user":"JesseM","date":". 05-26-2020, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","name":"JesseM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T12:25:13-07:00","id":1391746,"title":"","content":"A few of the signature characters have weird backgrounds like being from an abyssal version of our reality, or having their past erased from this timeline. It seems like a story you could do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">nd if he can; does anything stop him from thinking that if he's in the future there's a big chance this future won't be the one that becomes real so he'd better teleport back to the past and try and stick there as long as he can?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I mean, this is a road of paranoia that leads to insanity, so some sort of Mind magic would help, as would therapy and other ways to focus their mind on things other than worrying about the unwritten future. Basically exposing oneself to other things and pulling you out of the illogical logic circuit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you have a whole collective of the same mage from different potential futures living in the present and desperately trying to anchor themselves so they can live there permanently? </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It would speak of the type of mass insanity that might explain a Banisher legacy. Especially considering if the are using magic to anchor themselves, it's conceivable they could latch onto the idea that only other magic-users could dislodge them.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T15:37:58-07:00","id":1391796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JesseM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future?p=1391688#post1391688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording might suggest this rule only applies to time travelers themselves, and I think it would also cause all sorts of problems if every time you traveled to the past, part of the way you'd be altering history would be that practically every other mage community around the world would soon learn they were just living in a sort of draft version of an altered past (one which could be undone by locating the time traveler and dispelling the magic that brought them there, which is said in the core book to revert history to the original version).</div> </div> </div> </div>If they aren't examining something the time traveler has already interacted with \u2014 i.e. if the record of what they did has not had an opportunity to be derailed \u2014 then they are getting the same information they got originally. Without alteration, those spells return the same results they did when they were cast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391468-can-you-get-temporal-refugees-from-the-future?p=1391672#post1391672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff registering as being FROM the future isn't that weird. Any Time 3+ mage can pull that off. And it highlights them and their actions in BIG NEON SPOTLIGHTS in Time Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's being from the present while in the past. Everyone you interact with in the past is a recording that changes in response to interaction until the spell ends and settles the matter. Those big neon spotlights literally don't happen in the present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The part that confuses people is that they think that there's a single &quot;present&quot;. For the timetraveller, the &quot;present&quot; is the time they cast their time travelling spell, and they are in the past. For everyone else, the current time is the &quot;present&quot; and the time traveler shows signs of significant temporal distortion. </div> </div> </div>The way that Time works for mages' spells, the time traveler's present <i>is</i> the present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now something registering ITSELF as being IN or FROM the future , now that's weird. </div> </div> </div>See again: Atlantean ruins registering their ages and points of temporal origin as chronological impossibilities. Like being from a point in time that hasn't happened yet without the justification of Mage Sight revealing them as time travelers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}